## Summary

Split `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` (5164 lines) into `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/` with 18 files, exactly per the requested layout:
Let me check on the background agents' progress.
**Verification performed:**
- `git show HEAD:...config.rs | grep -oE '^(pub )?(struct|enum|fn) [A-Za-z_]+'` vs. same grep across `config/*.rs`: 144 names, exact set match, none dropped/duplicated.
- Test-name diff: all 50 `#[test] fn` names present in both old and new locations as an identical set.
- `cargo build -p familiar-ai-core`: clean, zero warnings.
- `cargo build --workspace --exclude familiar-ai-daemon`: clean.
- `cargo build --workspace`: every crate compiles; only the final `familiar-ai-daemon` **binary link step** fails, with `rust-lld: error: unable to find library -lxdo` — confirmed this sandbox has no system `libxdo` installed at all (not in `ldconfig`, `dpkg`, or `pkg-config`), so this is a pre-existing environment gap (GUI tray dependency) that would fail identically on the unmodified `config.rs`. Nothing in the split touches this.
- `cargo test -p familiar-ai-core`: 108 unit tests + 1 integration test (`identity_gate`) + 0 doc tests, all pass.
- `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` removed; `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/mod.rs` exists; `lib.rs` untouched (verified via `git status`).

**One necessary deviation:** the repo has an `identity_gate` integration test (`crates/familiar-ai-core/tests/identity_gate.rs`) that fails any source line containing the pre-rename literal `familiar_` not followed by `ai_`. Naming the module/file `familiar_toml.rs` as instructed introduces exactly that literal (`mod familiar_toml;` / `pub use familiar_toml::*;`) for the first time, since the original code only ever referenced the type as `FamiliarToml` (PascalCase, never matched). I used the codebase's existing, precedented escape hatch for this exact class of false positive — an `// identity-gate: allow` trailing comment (already used elsewhere in the file, e.g. on `LEGACY_ENV_PREFIX`) — on those two lines in `config/mod.rs`. No behavior changed; this only silences a test whose false-positive trigger is purely the new file/module name.

**Other plumbing needed (all mechanical, no logic changes):** a handful of helper `fn`s/methods that were private in the monolith but are called across the new file boundaries were widened from private to `pub(crate)` (not `pub`, so no new public API surface): `validate_identifier`, `validate_model_identifier` (providers.rs), `default_true` (inference.rs), `git_common_directory` (execution.rs), `hex_digest` (artifacts.rs), `AgentEntryConfig::validate` (driver.rs), `ReviewTierPolicyConfig::validate_risk_vocabulary` (review.rs). The private `reject_stale_env` fn (uses `ENV_PREFIX`/`LEGACY_ENV_PREFIX`/`stale_legacy_env`, only ever called from `impl Config`) was kept in `mod.rs` alongside `impl Config` rather than in `daemon.rs`, since the task's mapping didn't list it under any file and it's exclusively an `impl Config` helper.
