## Summary

The mechanical refactor extracting subcommand implementations out of `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/bin/familiar-ai.rs` is done and verified.

**Line counts:**
- `bin/familiar-ai.rs`: 2563 → 475 lines (now just top-level clap `Cli`/`Command` definitions, dispatch-only `main()`, `fail()`, and the existing `#[cfg(test)]` clap-parsing tests, unchanged).
- New modules under `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/bin/cli/` (21 files, ~2200 lines total): `mod.rs`, `backlog.rs`, `billing.rs`, `common.rs`, `compress.rs`, `config.rs`, `control.rs`, `deliver.rs`, `drive.rs`, `history.rs`, `next.rs`, `onboard.rs`, `plan.rs`, `preflight.rs`, `report.rs`, `resume.rs`, `run.rs`, `scope_decisions.rs`, `stewardship.rs`, `usage.rs`, `worker.rs`.

**One deliberate deviation from the task instructions:** the plan said to put the new tree at `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli/`, but that path collides with a pre-existing, unrelated `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli.rs` already used by this crate's *other* binary (`src/main.rs`, a small daemon-launch `Cli` struct). Since `main.rs`/`lib.rs` share `src/` as their module root, adding `src/cli/` there would conflict with the existing `mod cli;` (`cli.rs` vs `cli/mod.rs` ambiguity). The subagent instead placed the new tree at `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/bin/cli/`, which is exactly where Rust resolves `mod cli;` declared inside `src/bin/familiar-ai.rs` (binaries at `src/bin/<name>.rs` search their own `src/bin/` directory). This satisfies "dispatch-only binary + per-domain `cli/` modules with `mod cli;`" without touching the unrelated existing `cli.rs`.

**Verification (re-checked directly, not just trusting the subagent):**
- `cargo build -p familiar-ai-daemon --bin familiar-ai` — clean.
- `cargo test -p familiar-ai-daemon --no-default-features` — passes (255 total per subagent; spot-checked a slice, all green, 0 failed).
- `cargo build --workspace` succeeds under `--no-default-features`; under default features one pre-existing, unrelated failure exists (missing system lib `-lxdo` for the optional `tray` GUI feature on the *other* daemon binary) — confirmed unrelated to this change.
- `cargo fmt -p familiar-ai-daemon -- --check` clean.
- `--help` output (top-level + all first-level subcommands + a sample of second-level ones) diffed byte-identical before/after.
- One test file needed a mechanical update: `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/control_plane_boundaries.rs::legacy_cli_mutation_handlers_are_rendering_adapters_only` did raw text scans of the old monolithic binary file to check that certain handler functions don't inline scheduler/DB logic. Updated it to read the same functions from their new locations (`cli/resume.rs`, `cli/deliver.rs`, `cli/run.rs`, `cli/drive.rs`) with the identical forbidden-string checks — no assertions changed, just the source location scanned.
- `git status` confirms only `bin/familiar-ai.rs`, the new `bin/cli/` directory, and `tests/control_plane_boundaries.rs` were touched by this work; the concurrent `familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` → `config/` split and `docs/prds/*`/`docs/contracts/*` changes from other in-flight work were left untouched.

No commits were made, per the task instructions.
