## Summary

Implemented PRD-076 (Scope Modularization for Parallel Authoring) as a pure, behavior-preserving refactor:

1. **`config.rs` → `config/` module tree** — 17 per-feature files (`providers.rs`, `registry.rs`, `driver.rs`, `review.rs`, `execution.rs`, `delivery.rs`, `daemon.rs`, `inference.rs`, etc.) re-exported unchanged from `mod.rs`. Added a pinned fixture-configuration test (`config::tests::pinned_fixture_configuration_resolves_identically_across_the_module_split`) as the equivalence oracle spanning most modules.
2. **`docs/contracts/providers.md` → `docs/contracts/providers/`** — index + `inference-providers.md`, `credential-authentication.md`, `registry-migration.md`, content moved verbatim per section.
3. **CLI binary thinned** — `bin/familiar-ai.rs` dropped from 2563 → 475 lines (dispatch-only); subcommand bodies moved to 21 new modules under `bin/cli/` (had to land at `src/bin/cli/` rather than `src/cli/` due to a pre-existing unrelated `cli.rs` for the daemon's own binary — documented in the plan).
4. **10 pending PRDs amended** (038, 053, 058–063, 071–073) to narrow `expected_files` to specific per-feature files instead of shared surfaces; PRD-080 was already narrow. PRD-076's own declaration corrected to match the real `bin/cli/` path.
5. **New pinned regression test** `crates/familiar-ai-review/tests/scope_narrowing.rs` (12 tests) pins every amendment and computationally proves the scheduler's own conflict rule now gives wave 5 (038/053/058) an achievable width of 2.
6. **`EXECUTION-PLAN.md` regenerated** with real computed widths and an explicit, honest note that wave 6 remains at width 1 because `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/` and `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/` stay as shared whole-directory declarations — out of this PRD's authorized scope (same precedent as `billing.rs` being left to PRD-052/054).

**Verification**: full workspace build and test suite green (65/65 result blocks, one known pre-existing timing-flaky test confirmed to pass in isolation), `cargo fmt --check` clean, `cargo clippy` shows only two pre-existing warnings in untouched files, CLI `--help` output byte-identical before/after (verified via `git stash -u`), and `backlog metadata-check --advisory` exits 0 with no diagnostics.
